  "_comment": "Phase 225 plan 06 (CONN-03, MT5D-08). The cross-runtime oracle for the broker-server identity rule. Read by src/lib/venue-identity.test.ts (normaliseVenueServer, sameVenueServer, pickSameAccountHolder) and analytics-service/tests/test_venue_server_identity.py (normalise_venue_server, same_venue_server, pick_same_account_holder). HAND-TYPED: every expectation below was worked out by hand from the rule, never produced by either implementation, and every id and server is synthetic. The rule. NORMALISE: trim only space, tab, CR and LF from both ends (the SQL btrim(x, E' \\t\\r\\n') of swap_account_slot and api_keys_venue_server_valid, so a vertical tab or a no-break space is NOT trimmed, in all three places), lower-case, blank becomes null, more than 128 characters after trimming becomes null, anything that is not a string becomes null. SAME: two servers are the same account when both are equal OR when EITHER is null (a key not yet backfilled matches on login alone). PICK: among the live keys of one login, tier 1 is a row whose server equals the new key's server (null equals null), tier 2 is a row where either side is null, tier 3 exists only in mode after_index_refusal (the old login-only index refused the write) and takes any row; the first non-empty tier wins and inside it the smallest id by plain string comparison, so the pick never depends on row order. ASCII letters only in the case-folded cases: JS toLowerCase, Python lower and SQL lower differ on a few non-ASCII code points. CONNECT (end to end, WR-03): the stored server for a RAW connect-time passphrase. The Python seam strips the raw value with str.strip() (parse_mt5_credentials) BEFORE the poll normalises it, so the TS connect routes strip the same set first (normaliseConnectedVenueServer). That set is Python's isspace(): tab to CR, U+001C to U+0020, U+0085, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000 to U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000. It is NOT JavaScript's trim(): U+FEFF is kept and U+001C to U+001F and U+0085 are stripped, so the U+0085 and U+FEFF cases below tell the two apart where a no-break space alone would not. Python replays each case through the real parse_mt5_credentials then _mt5_session_server; TS through normaliseConnectedVenueServer. A raw value that is only whitespace has no case because the Python seam refuses it. TOKENS (225 plan 14, CONTEXT Q6): the account identity token of each key, and the ambiguous key ids, for a key set of one owner. Read by analytics-service/tests/test_venue_server_identity.py (account_identity_tokens, ambiguous_server_key_ids) in the order given and reversed, and by src/lib/venue-identity.test.ts. The rule: login is venue_account_id stripped (a blank login has no login identity); server is venue_server when it is a non-empty string, read as stored (nothing trimmed or case-folded); for each (exchange case-blind, login) S is the set of distinct servers among the keys given; a key's canonical server is its own, else the empty server when S is empty, else the single member when S has one member, else NONE and the key is AMBIGUOUS. Two keys share a token when (exchange, login, canonical server) are equal, the token is account:<smallest id by plain string comparison>; an ambiguous key takes part in no login union and has a null token unless a duplicate or composite_member marker links it; a marker union is unchanged. ambiguous lists the keys with a login, no server and two or more servers on the login, marker or not. Do not add a case here without its expectation; both suites consume this file whole and assert every array is non-empty.",
